# Recompiled with `--exclude-newer 2026-09-23T00:00:00Z` and `--no-header`
# (see .github/workflows/hardware-profile-smoke.yml, where both the committed
# lock generation and the CI diff-check recompile pass the same cutoff; the
# lock file itself carries no header comment) so CI's redundant-compile-and-diff
# check stays deterministic over time: without a cutoff, any transitive
# dependency publishing a new release after this file was generated would
# make uv resolve a different set and fail the diff on every unrelated pull
# request.
